PURPOSE
H95 showed:
shadow developmental rehearsal
can replace much live experimentation,

but:
one stale model can create:
a closed self-confirming loop.

H96 asks:

SHOULD THE ORGANISM MAINTAIN
SEVERAL SMALL SHADOW SELF-MODELS

and spend:
REAL EVIDENCE

when:
those models disagree?

The critical negative is:

WHAT IF ALL MODELS
SHARE THE SAME BLIND SPOT?

BOUNDARY
This is synthetic.

It does not:
- freeze three shadow models;
- freeze disagreement threshold = 1 step;
- prove real model families have independent error provenance;
- freeze audit-floor probability;
- modify or execute STAB-18-R1.

