COMPARATORS

FIXED RANDOM CALIBRATION
3% real calibration when:
shadow would not develop.

No disagreement trigger.

DISAGREEMENT ONLY

real evidence only when:
model SD > threshold.

DISAGREEMENT + SMALL RANDOM FLOOR

same
plus:
1% random real-audit floor.

PERFECT-ish MEDIAN
upper bound:
three nearly accurate models.

PROVENANCE-DIVERSE ENSEMBLE
For the common-bias stress,
the three shadow models are instead given:
different structural inductive biases.

Their initial predictions become approximately:

3.5,
7.0,
9.5

for true:
3.

This represents:
failure-mode diversity

rather than:
three copies of one predictor.

